<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="section-riemann-sums-and-integrals" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Riemann Sums and Integrals
  </title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      In this section, we construct the <term> Riemann integral </term> as a limit of <term> Riemann sums </term>. We prove several equivalent characterizations of integrability and explore some preliminary properties of integration.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="./subsection-finite-integration-methods.ptx"/>

  <xi:include href="./subsection-riemann-integrability.ptx"/>

  <conclusion>
    <p>
      In the next section, we will relate the processes of differentiation and integration. Along the way, we will find ways to compute Riemann integrals without computing Riemann sums and discover anti-derivatives of continuous functions.
    </p>
  </conclusion>

  <xi:include href="./exercises-riemann-sums-and-integrals.ptx"/>

  <xi:include href="./problems-riemann-sums-and-integrals.ptx"/>
</section>
